# MealHQ delivery standards (FE)

Before marking **any** UI behavior-changing task complete:

1. Follow the development loop (plan → clean → implement → test → re-verify → context sync).
2. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/mealhq-ui-screen/SKILL.md`.
3. API-first when an endpoint exists; then one Browser MCP smoke (≤5 calls) on the focus URL; always `browser_close_tab`.
4. Run production **build** for the touched app **after** UI QA (never mid-QA).
5. Context sync via sibling `mealhq-api/.cursor/skills/mealhq-context-sync/SKILL.md` before Done.
6. Update FE docs if copy/behavior changes; if API contract changes, update mealhq-api docs same change set.

## Completion message must include

- **Test tier** / what was verified
- **Build** command + pass/fail
- **Browser MCP** line (Pass/Fail/Skipped with reason)
- **Context sync** line

## Do not

- Mark Done with “servers not up” — start FE and sibling API
- Skip Browser MCP for user-facing UI (unless user forbade browser in this chat)
- Invent Phase 2 inbox / WhatsApp chat UI
- Commit / deploy / PR unless the user explicitly asked
